  "claim_scope": "Candidate C5 (wave A): registered-empty fragment producers for EXTERNAL_CUSTODY and PROOF_REWARDS, pure functions of the committed lane root that certify the lane is disabled and committed at the root of its unique empty typed lane state (ExternalCustodyDisabledStateV1, ProofRewardsPolicyBlockedStateV1) in Python and Rust, with three closed reject codes; the certificate checker binds registered-empty lanes to those roots (REGISTERED_EMPTY_ROOT_DRIFT, 15 codes, 27 vectors). Candidate C4d (Opus P10 repairs): a pending external obligation repeated across lanes rejects (both implementations, Rust unit gate), the lane-binding checks are check-major so the declared precedence is the realised one (new vector), the dead AllocationClassV1 enum is removed from the module and the canonical manifest, and the fixture surface is total. Candidate C4c: the bounded ESSO model (two lanes, one domain, two claimants, eight atoms per cell) is an inductive two-solver contract for the certificate relation with eight invariants including the derived normative partition and same-domain backing, eight named mutants each attributed to one invariant, and a runtime link to the Python checker. Candidate C4b: the bounded Lean model (three lanes, two domains, two claimants over natural numbers) derives the normative partition, same-domain backing, open-terminal coverage, the exact current-profile custody special case, and the registered-empty-only consequence of having no receipt-backed producer, and refutes reserve masking, unassigned atoms, producer-less enabled lanes, and over-entitled terminal claims; bound by its own compile/axioms/pin gate and by the O-008 packet as a second Lean subject. Candidate C4a: GlobalAccountingAllocationCertificateV1, the state-keyed sidecar checker over the control-domain vocabulary (claimant entitlements, unencumbered reserves, pending external obligations, terminal bindings) with a producer registry exhaustive over the twelve lanes (EXTERNAL_CUSTODY registered-empty-disabled, PROOF_REWARDS registered-empty-blocked, ten NO_PRODUCER lanes blocked on their unresolved policies), fourteen closed reject codes in fixed check precedence, checked u128 folds, derived field-ownership/terminal-binding/allocation roots, and a Python/Rust twin replaying one rendered twenty-five-vector golden fixture (three accepts: registered-empty over empty state, acknowledged outbox, drained terminal; one reject per reachable code; root-pinning synthetic fragments). Research-only: no lane producer is receipt-backed, nothing is mounted, and the reject-is-no-op contract is asserted on state roots.",
